From t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk  Fri Jul  4 11:42:03 2014
From: t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk (Jombart, Thibaut)
Date: Fri, 4 Jul 2014 09:42:03 +0000
Subject: [adegenet-forum] Importing Z (X) linked data?
In-Reply-To: <597CEF26-8015-4483-A12E-2E179091EBC3@bu.edu>
References: <597CEF26-8015-4483-A12E-2E179091EBC3@bu.edu>
Message-ID: <2CB2DA8E426F3541AB1907F98ABA65709A12F955@icexch-m1.ic.ac.uk>


Hi there,

if you have a mixture of haploid/diploid genotypes, then you'd need to recode all as diploid, and then convert the data to genind (e.g. using df2genind). Note that the allele frequencies at a population level will be wrong. But individual-level multivariate analyses (PCA, PCoA, DAPC etc) will be OK

Cheers
Thibaut
